        Nicotine pouches are legal in most European countries as of 2026. They are not classified as tobacco products under the EU Tobacco Products Directive because they contain no tobacco leaf. Some countries have introduced specific regulations: Belgium has banned them, Denmark is implementing strength caps (April 2026), and Norway has banned them outright (including import). Finland allows in-store sales only — distance selling is prohibited. The Netherlands is fully legal. The EU TPD3 revision (expected 2028+) may introduce EU-wide rules.
      </p>
    </div>

